## Notes and approximations

- Features at hour h use real detections at h plus everything known from earlier hours; labels use the gap-filled table.
- Hours whose fire is entirely gap-filled (64 fire-hours) or that have no satellite data make no rows.
- 'Fire centre' (for downwind) and the mean fire elevation use ALL squares burning in the 80 km box, so a second
  fire in the box pulls the centre towards it.
- growth_last_hour_km2 counts real detections in both hours; it is NaN at hour 0 or after a no-data hour.
- burning_within_4km counts the square itself if it is burning; burning_neighbours does not.
- frp_now_mw adds up the squares that have a power value (GOES gives no power for some fire pixels).
- Squares near the box edge have fewer neighbours inside the box; fire outside the box is not seen.
- Weather is one point per fire (its start point), the same for every square in an hour.
- nearest_town_* columns are for warnings only - NOT model features. Do not train on them or on the ID columns.

